 "printed_length": {
  "lines": 193,
  "left_sub_column": 97,
  "right_sub_column": 96,
  "letters_waiting": 218,
  "how_the_letters_were_counted": "One letter to a line, plus the trailing digit where the list prints one: fifteen lines carry a `2` and one carries a `3` in the left sub-column, four carry a `2` and two a `3` in the right. 193 + 17 + 8 = 218.",
  "the_printed_total": {
   "as_printed": "21[8]",
   "stands": "at the foot of the right sub-column, right-aligned above the postmaster's signature",
   "read": 218,
   "why_the_last_digit_is_bracketed": "The figure stands hard against the column rule and its third digit is inked thin: read alone it is an 8 with a faint left side, and 6 and 5 are not excluded by the glyph. What settles it is that the roster's own tally of the 193 lines and their letter-count digits is 218 exactly, derived line by line and without reference to this figure. THAT IS A CHECK AND NOT A PROOF, and it is written this way round on purpose: the tally is the measurement, the printed figure agrees with it, and the digit is left bracketed because the type does not carry it cleanly. `--check` re-derives the tally and fails if it stops being 218."
  },
  "addressee_lines_that_are_firms": [],
